Subject: Show the greeter on a Switch User display, on a VT of its own, and return to an autologin session

With Autologin.Relogin=true every new display logs the autologin account
in, the one SeatManager::switchToGreeter makes for Switch User included, and
that login fails on a seat the account's session already holds. The Switch
User display skips the autologin and shows the greeter.

fetchAvailableVt() asks whether "ttySDDM_INITIAL_VT" is in use:
SDDM_INITIAL_VT is a static const int, which the preprocessor cannot
stringify, so the initial VT always looks free and a second display takes
the VT of the running session. The name is built at run time instead.

A password typed at that greeter returns to the account's own session only
when that session's PAM service is "sddm"; a session that began as an
autologin ("sddm-autologin") is not found, and the login starts a second
session for the same account. Both services are matched.

